Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:32:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] ogsf: the depth range of the view, and the eye separation
 that fits limits

GS_get_depth_range() reads the distances of the nearest and the farthest
pixel the last drawing left in the viewport, and GS_get_stereo_separation()
gives the largest separation of the eyes under which every distance between
them stays inside a sunk and a popped limit, in pixels of the view.  The
separation GS_set_eye_separation() takes is now a fraction of the distance to
the focus point.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
